class V = a e i o u y aa ee ii oo uu eu ai au
class C = p t k b d g m n r l s z f v h w j ch zh sh th dh gh

:: Grimm's law (first phase) — Voiceless stops become fricatives: p t k > f th h. (Proto-Germanic, c. 500 BC)
p > f
t > th
k > h

:: Verner's law (simplified) — Medial fricatives voice between vowels (the full law is conditioned on accent; this is the vowel-context core). (Proto-Germanic, c. 400 BC)
f > v / V _ V
th > dh / V _ V
s > z / V _ V
h > g / V _ V
